Wumpuses... Wumpi.... Whatever. Anyway, the game was a group of up to
say, 100 room. (I think it depended on the number of players) with
random links among them. If a wumpus was in an adjoining room, it
would say that there were tracks to such and such a cave number.
You would have a choice of moving to another cave/room or shooting
an arrow. You would either eventually kill all the Wumpuses, or die
when one came storming over from an adjacent room. Oh well,
enough reminicing.

BTW, re: Friday 13, I reset the clock on my system at home to said
date. Played a few games. Didn't pray until around move 2500. Was
'piously aligned' or some such. My god wasn't interested. Tried
this on a couple or three games.  There does _definitely_ seem
to be something more to the 13th than just the normal new moon
bad luck. (Yes, I've played the game enough to have a feel
for when you can/can't pray. :-)

One last thing, in refrence to the text file about the hack to
nethack (the next generation, or some such).  The bit about
changing the names of monsters on the rogue level certainly
brought back some memories. Thanks...

